      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A composite picture of the natural history of coronary disease has emerged from a large prospective study of patients who were followed for periods ranging from seven to 13 years. The course of the disease as reflected in the data appears more favorable than that predicted from retrospective studies, with respect to both mortality and quality of life."},
